## DBsubject('Introductory Statistics')
## DBchapter('1')
## DBsection('1')
## Author('Michael Stassen')
## Institution('Fitchburg State University')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'parserPopUp.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

@opts = (
    'number of competing computer spreadsheet software packages',
    "Level of education (high school, some college, associate's, etc.)",
    'age of executives in Fortune 500 companies (years)',
    'number of students enrolled at Fitchburg State',
    'number of tickets sold to a concert',
    'brand of toothpaste',
    'most-watched television show',
    'time in line to buy groceries (minutes)',
    'favorite baseball team',
);

@types = (
    'Categorical-Ordinal',  'Categorical-Nominal',
    'Numerical-Continuous', 'Numerical-Discrete'
);

@answers = (3, 0, 3, 3, 3, 1, 1, 2, 1);

@slice = random_subset(scalar(@opts), 0 .. $#opts);

@dd = map { DropDown([ [@types] ], $answers[$_], labels => 'ABC') } @slice;

BEGIN_PGML
Identify the type of data for each variable:

a) [$opts[$slice[0]]] [_]{$dd[0]}
a) [$opts[$slice[1]]] [_]{$dd[1]}
a) [$opts[$slice[2]]] [_]{$dd[2]}
a) [$opts[$slice[3]]] [_]{$dd[3]}
a) [$opts[$slice[4]]] [_]{$dd[4]}
a) [$opts[$slice[5]]] [_]{$dd[5]}
a) [$opts[$slice[6]]] [_]{$dd[6]}
a) [$opts[$slice[7]]] [_]{$dd[7]}
a) [$opts[$slice[8]]] [_]{$dd[8]}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

Recall that 
* A *categorical* variable is non numeric.  The values are categories
    - An *ordinal* categorical variable can be ranked. 
    - A *nomial* categorical variable cannot be ranked.
* A *numerical* variable take on numbers as values. 
    - A *discrete* variable is a whole number (0,1,2,...)
    - A *continuous* variable can take on any number between the whole numbers.  Examples include weight, distance and time:

a) [$opts[$slice[0]]] [$dd[0]]
a) [$opts[$slice[1]]] [$dd[1]]
a) [$opts[$slice[2]]] [$dd[2]]
a) [$opts[$slice[3]]] [$dd[3]]
a) [$opts[$slice[4]]] [$dd[4]]
a) [$opts[$slice[5]]] [$dd[5]]
a) [$opts[$slice[6]]] [$dd[6]]
a) [$opts[$slice[7]]] [$dd[7]]
a) [$opts[$slice[8]]] [$dd[8]]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
